The Options.txt is in `Live 12.3.6` but you're likely running **Live 12.4.3** (the latest). The file needs to be in the correct version's folder. Let's put it in all the Live 12.4.x folders:

```powershell
@("Live 12.4", "Live 12.4.1", "Live 12.4.2", "Live 12.4.3") | ForEach-Object {
    $dir = "$env:APPDATA\Ableton\$_\Preferences"
    if (Test-Path $dir) {
        Set-Content -Path "$dir\Options.txt" -Value "-_PluginAutoPopulateThreshold=128"
        Write-Host "Created Options.txt in $_"
    }
}
```

Then restart Ableton. That should do it.

